<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικ-ιστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοῖνιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>dyer of purple</i> or <i>red,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> among the Persians,
				<i>wearer of purple,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλουργής</span> (q. v.), i.e. <i>one of the highest
				rank,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.2.20
			</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοινικίζων</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				883
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				235.47
			</span></i>.</div>
